{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1448087-how-do-toreadors-and-ventrue-hide-their-immortality","id":1448087,"title":"How do Toreadors and Ventrue hide their immortality?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-05-09T18:44:45-07:00","id":1448087,"title":"How do Toreadors and Ventrue hide their immortality?","content":"Toreadors interact with a fairly small group of rich people on a routine basis both as artists and as rich patrons of the arts. And vampires, excluding Gangrel, are supposedly almost never nomadic, remaining in one city for centuries. Does no one notice that the same person has been throwing parties for the avant guard every week for 30 years and hasn't aged a day?<br /> <br /> Ditto for Ventrue. Does no one notice that the same person has been throwing cocktail parties for politicians and businessmen for 30 years and hasn't aged a day?<br /> <br /> It's something that's bothered me for years, and I was reminded of it while playing Coteries of New York. Your mentor gets into a bit of trouble because the nosy guy discovers evidence that the same person has been a patron of the arts for decades. You resolve the situation fairly casually, but really this should be a huge, constant problem for any vampire who needs to routinely interact with a significant number of mortals in order to maintain their influence. And you can't just vanish for 20 years and come back as your son/daughter, because then you lose that domain and need to survive not having it for decades, and then need to claw your way back into having it again from whoever claimed it in the meantime.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-09T19:17:47-07:00","id":1448090,"title":"","content":"For most of history this wasn't really that much of a problem (esp. with some Disciplines to help out).<br /> <br /> It's really not that hard though. Some hair dye for big events to make it look like your hair is greying over the years. People will ask about your skin care routine, but you play coy. Eventually you fake your death, have a ghoul run things for a bit. Then come back as your kid or grand-kid that's a striking image of you but clearly looks younger than when you &quot;passed&quot; away. Rinse and repeat every few decades.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-09T22:09:57-07:00","id":1448097,"title":"","content":"Vampires fake their death regularly and legaly their money is not owed by themselves but by ghouls or foundations they control<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24037-leandro16","name":"Leandro16","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24037_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-09T23:04:06-07:00","id":1448100,"title":"","content":"Indeed, though I'd say the -fake death- gets a bit inconvenient in modern times where plenty of people are living a century. Faking your death for 40+ years is tough, do you send assassins around to kill your old friends and speed the process along? <br /> I think all vampires should try to gain obfuscate at some point so they can put up many masks and hold different personas. You can't do this in V5 because Mask's a 4th or 5th level ability and too expensive, but in the rest of VtM it's a mere 31xp to get obfuscate 3 OoC and they can probably manage that before the second persona needs to fake their death (Toreador and Ventrue are generally good perfomers so don't need to buy the related skills) <br /> Sabbat have Vicissitude. <br /> <br /> <br /> One radical idea, is that in the WoD, extending your age through arcane power isn't that weird in the upper circles. Between vampires, infernalists, mages, strange weaver and wyrm superproducts, and other, stranger solutions, it's not too weird to have elite multi-millionaires and billionaires last longer and look better than they should. These people keep quiet about the crimes their friends are committing IRL, so it's not much of a stretch to believe they'd be quiet about some folks living longer than they should. They'd likely have rules about this sorta thing; nobody gets to be high profile and immortal. <br /> Give it a couple decades and perhaps someone real will work out how to make us unaging like lobsters or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-10T01:51:40-07:00","id":1448107,"title":"","content":"Maintaning the mask of a celebrity artist or wealthy businessman is much more problematic in the age of Facebook and Instagram than in nights past, and I imagine it is increasingly discouraged among the Camarilla. However as others have noted, the methods of fabricating and eventually retiring a mortal identity are tried-and-true. The Blood Bond creates willing accomplices, money purchases privacy, and retainers can handle the minutiae of inheritance, records and other details. <br /> <br /> It's worth pointing out that in the World of Darkness, Vampires have had a hand in the inner workings of society for literal millennia. All the institutions---government, church, the courts, the press, high society---are thoroughly corrupt and well-greased to facilitate whatever ends old and influential Kindred might put them to. Younger vampires, of course, must either make their own way or resort to their elders for help with such matters, and that is one more way in which the ancients can keep their childer in line. <br /> <br /> It's one more way in which the divide between High Clan and Low Clan--even if those terms are now archaic--are enforced. The Disciplines of Ventrue and Toreador facilitate the manipulation of society. Ensconsing themselves in such circles comes easy and naturally and the influence over the canaille they can work reflects their influence in the Society of the Damned. The debilities of other Clans makes it harder for them, and thus stealth or distance is the naturally preferred solution.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26710-ventrue-busboy","name":"Ventrue Busboy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26710_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-10T06:45:35-07:00","id":1448121,"title":"","content":"this really isn't such an issue as you think. just because one of your identities has to be dead doesn't mean you can't exert influence over your domain, you still got ghouls, false identities and corporations so you can operate things from behind the scenes. also there's such a thing as a disguise which doesn't have to be so extensive that you need viscitude so you can still walk through the streets without worrying about being recognized. and they can still do business with other kindred too.<br /> <br /> that is assuming of course that said kindred are public figures which most kindred aren't (including most ventrue and toreadors)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25992-archderd","name":"archderd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-10T07:21:02-07:00","id":1448124,"title":"","content":"Also bear in mind that if you\u2019re a celebrity vampire and are spotted after your death, as long as it\u2019s low key it\u2019ll have all the credibility of an Elvis sighting. In fact, the bigger a spectacle you can make out of your \u201cdeath\u201d the easier that\u2019ll be.<br /> <br /> Taking 3 rounds to the chest or getting your throat slit aren\u2019t actually lethal to vampires... but having either happen on live TV sells the idea that \u201cYup, they\u2019re dead\u201d in a way that makes any post-mortem sighting in a hoodie and dark glasses only fit for the tabloids.<br /> <br /> Another point is that the clever vampire would start setting up their next life well ahead of the demise of their current one. Go with the subtle aging makeup (adding glasses helps too) and become more reclusive over the course of a few decades and then start sending your \u201cson\u201d or \u201cdaughter\u201d out to handle \u201cfamily business\u201d whenever you\u2019re meeting someone new. A half-dozen years after that \u201cmom\u201d or \u201cdad\u201d retires entirely and half-a-dozen after that you bring out an elderly blood bound (but not perma-ghouled, just enough to keep them bound) and/or domnated body double to pretend to be you for another dozen years until they finally pass on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-12T13:34:32-07:00","id":1448354,"title":"","content":"In the case of bureaucratic and governmental entities, one can simply just not be a person. For Ventrue, at least in the United States, it's easy. The US recognizes corporations as people; therefore one is not Mr. Ventrue but rather Ventrue Enterprises. For Toreador, the become the Toreador Foundation for the Arts, a non-profit organization. As for individual interactions, one doesn't schmooze the politician directly - his wife, his secretary, his aide are all influential to him, maybe even as influential as the big donation from the Ventrue Corp.<br /> <br /> Cheers!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-14T19:23:31-07:00","id":1448561,"title":"","content":"They don't; most vampires die out before their mortal life-spans; it takes real poise to see a century.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"738"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}